window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-a3395850043efc03"]={"key":"ny_main-a3395850043efc03","group":"ny_main","uid":"a3395850043efc03","rank":57,"title":"sheafield drakemoor case response copy 001","occupation":"order_clerks","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are an order clerk at Sheafield Works supporting Cormac Voskresensky on the Drakemoor Health Network account. Drakemoor has challenged a short-shipment charge for a temperature-controlled component because the same affected units appear once as rejected and again as returned, and Carsten Hartnett is waiting for a written resolution. Tamsin Beaulieu has already documented the correction authority, but Ruben Jaramillo cannot release the replacement planned for Monday until the corrected account position and the delivery-cutoff decision are clear. Work only from `Drakemoor_case_packet.docx`, which consolidates the correspondence, the case activity extract, the carrier timing evidence supplied by Nils Rasmussen, and the applicable correction and release note. Give me back one workbook named `Drakemoor_case_response.xlsx`, written at the top level of the working directory you start in using exactly that filename. Use exactly three worksheets named `Case Response`, `Evidence`, and `Release Plan`. Please make the workbook do the following: (1) give the `Case Response` sheet a concise case summary showing the customer, case, account, original shipment, replacement shipment, affected component, dispute reason, authorized correction, recommended interpretation of the cutoff evidence, resulting headline amount due, and recommended release status; (2) present a clean, chronological evidence record on `Evidence`, using consistent customer and shipment identifiers, retaining the case-line key and a source label, and representing each physical case line only once even when the packet uses more than one status description for it; (3) document the correction authorization accurately, including its reference, authorizer, unconditional correction, any correction that depends on the cutoff decision, and the resulting account position; (4) compare both reasonable readings of the carrier timing evidence, showing the amount due and replacement-release outcome if the recorded scan time controls and if the documented physical-attempt time controls; (5) choose one of those readings for the headline response and give a brief, source-based reason for the choice—either reading is acceptable, but the recommendation, amount due, customer wording, and release instruction must all follow the same choice; (6) include a customer-ready response to Carsten Hartnett of no more than 225 words that states what was found, what correction is authorized, the remaining amount due, and what will happen with the replacement without exposing unnecessary internal commentary; and (7) provide an executable `Release Plan` with an owner, action, trigger or dependency, due time, and completion evidence for approval, correction posting, account verification and shipment release, and customer communication. Include a method and assumptions note of no more than 175 words explaining the identifier treatment, how overlapping case lines were handled, and which cutoff interpretation drives the headline. Do not invent missing events, amounts, approvals, or commitments. Keep monetary values to cents, make dates and times unambiguous, ensure all displayed calculations agree across the workbook, and leave no spreadsheet error values in the finished file. Format the workbook so Cormac can review the decision quickly and Ruben can act from the release plan without having to reinterpret it.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/Drakemoor_case_packet.docx` — Consolidated case record containing the stakeholder correspondence, case activity extract, carrier timing evidence, correction authorization, and shipment-release terms.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `Drakemoor_case_response.xlsx` — Customer case response workbook reconciling the evidence, documenting the authorized correction, comparing cutoff interpretations, and providing shipment-release actions. (Place the file at the top level of the working directory.; Use exactly the worksheets Case Response, Evidence, and Release Plan.; Customer-ready response must not exceed 225 words.; Method and assumptions note must not exceed 175 words.; All monetary values must be shown to cents.; The workbook must contain no spreadsheet error values.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/Drakemoor_case_packet.docx","bytes":41837,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/89078604ad09ed057e2b44136a70a992e7bd52dd24e18b2f4872322b555f4247.docx","sha256":"89078604ad09ed057e2b44136a70a992e7bd52dd24e18b2f4872322b555f4247","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Drakemoor Health Network\nAccount review packet | temperature-controlled short-shipment dispute\nCustomer account\nDMH-Q47\nCase reference\nCASE-N64P\nOriginal shipment\nSHF-T83K\nAffected component\nTCV-9K temperature-controlled component | 31 units\nReplacement staged\nSHF-R77M | TCV-9K | batch BATCH-R52 | 31 units\n1. Stakeholder correspondence\nThread retained with the account record. Times below are local.\nFrom\nCarsten Hartnett | Drakemoor Health Network\nSent\n2026-11-11 09:18 local\nTo\nCormac Voskresensky | Sheafield Works\nSubject\nCASE-N64P / short-shipment charge\nCormac, the 31 TCV-9K temperature-controlled units from SHF-T83K appear once as rejected at receiving and again as returned to carrier. We do not see two physical sets of units. Please correct the charge and confirm what that means for the replacement requested for Monday.\n\nFrom\nRuben Jaramillo | Sheafield Works\nSent\n2026-11-12 08:06 local\nTo\nCormac Voskresensky; Tamsin Beaulieu\nSubject\nReplacement staging for Drakemoor\nSHF-R77M is staged for Monday, 2026-11-16: 31 TCV-9K components from batch BATCH-R52. I need the corrected account position and Cormac's approved response before I can release it.\n\nFrom\nCormac Voskresensky | Sheafield Works\nSent\n2026-11-12 09:08 local\nTo\nTamsin Beaulieu; Ruben Jaramillo\nSubject\nCorrection authority and cutoff review\nPlease document the correction authority and keep the timing issue tied to the carrier record. I will approve the case response once the account position and replacement instruction are clear.\n\n2. Case activity extract\nCase activity, queue 04 | exported 2026-11-12 08:39 local\nEvent #\nlogged (local)\nCust ID\nshipment_ID\nCase / line / disp.\nstatus_text\nQty Shipped\nAmount\nqueue\nACT-1179\n2026-11-10 17:04\nDMH-Q47\nSHF-T83K\nCASE-N64P / OL-V29 / DSP-H91\nRejected at receiving\n31\n$5,893.42\nrecon\nACT-1180\n2026-11-10 17:05\ndmh-q47 \nshf-t83k \nCASE-N64P / OL-V29 / DSP-H91\nReturned to carrier\n31\n$5,893.42\n\nACT-1183\n2026-11-12 08:39\n\n\n\nAnalyst adjusted amount preview\n\n#VALUE!\ncalc\nMatching used by this export: trim account and shipment fields and compare without regard to letter case. The case-line key carries customer account, shipment identifier, case reference, order line and disposition reference.\n3. Carrier timing evidence\nReceived from Nils Rasmussen, carrier liaison | all times local\nShipment / case\nSHF-T83K / CASE-N64P\nStated local cutoff\n2026-11-10 16:47\nHandheld physical attempt\n2026-11-10 16:44\nCentral recorded scan\n2026-11-10 16:51\nNils Rasmussen's message\nThe handheld captured the physical attempt before cutoff and synchronized to the central record afterward.\nApplicable wording\nAn attempted delivery must be completed and recorded no later than the stated local cutoff.\n\n\n4. Correction and release note\nTamsin Beaulieu | Account Specialist | 2026-11-12 11:48 local\nDecision reference\nACR-L53D\nAuthorizer\nTamsin Beaulieu, Account Specialist\nAccount at review\n$14,263.88 amount due\nCorrection 1\nAuthorize a $5,893.42 correction for the same physical CASE-N64P / OL-V29 / DSP-H91 line shown under both receiving-reject and carrier-return status. This correction is not dependent on the cutoff reading.\nCorrection 2\nAuthorize a further $3,147.68 timing correction only if the delivery attempt meets the stated cutoff condition.\nRelease terms\nAfter approved corrections are posted and Cormac Voskresensky approves the response, Ruben Jaramillo may release the replacement only if the remaining amount due is at or below $7,251.00.\nCommitted workflow\nCommitment\nOwner\nDue (local)\nDependency\nApprove case response\nCormac Voskresensky\n2026-11-13 12:37\nCorrection authority reviewed\nPost authorized correction; record ACR-L53D\nTamsin Beaulieu\n2026-11-13 14:23\nCormac approval\nSend approved response to Carsten Hartnett\nCormac Voskresensky\n2026-11-13 16:09\nPosting confirmation\nVerify corrected amount\nRuben Jaramillo\n2026-11-16 08:41\nApproved corrections posted\nRelease SHF-R77M\nRuben Jaramillo\n2026-11-16 09:17\nApproval and posting complete; amount due at or below $7,251.00\nClose the sequence with the Cormac approval record, the ACR-L53D posting reference, the balance-verification entry, the replacement release record, and the customer-send confirmation.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/Drakemoor_case_response.xlsx","bytes":14589,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/4f2f09bc8449a6f88b2404d56c7c896d6c01020c939c73378c80ed9b9d38207f.xlsx","sha256":"4f2f09bc8449a6f88b2404d56c7c896d6c01020c939c73378c80ed9b9d38207f","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Case Response","row_count":31,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["SHEAFIELD WORKS | CUSTOMER CASE RESPONSE","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Drakemoor Health Network | CASE-N64P | Decision prepared for Cormac Voskresensky","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["SELECTED DECISION","","","","","","HEADLINE AMOUNT DUE","","","RECOMMENDED RELEASE","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Use documented physical-attempt time: 2026-11-10 16:44 local. It precedes the stated cutoff of 2026-11-10 16:47 local.","","","","","","5222.78","","","RELEASE AFTER PRECONDITIONS\nApproval, posting, and Ruben's balance verification required.","",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"8","cells":["CASE SUMMARY","","","","","","CORRECTION AUTHORIZATION","","","","",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["Customer","","Drakemoor Health Network","","","","Authorization reference","","ACR-L53D","","",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["Customer account","","DMH-Q47","","","","Authorizer","","Tamsin Beaulieu","","",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["Case / original shipment","","CASE-N64P | SHF-T83K","","","","Opening amount due","","14263.88","","",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["Replacement shipment","","SHF-R77M | Monday, 2026-11-16","","","","Unconditional correction","","5893.42","","",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["Affected component","","TCV-9K temperature-controlled component | 31 units | batch BATCH-R52","","","","Cutoff-dependent correction","","3147.68","","",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["Dispute reason","","One physical line is described as both \"Rejected at receiving\" and \"Returned to carrier\".","","","","Resulting account position","","5222.78","","",""]},{"r":"17","cells":["CUTOFF INTERPRETATION COMPARISON","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["Cutoff interpretation","Evidence reading","","","Unconditional correction","Timing correction","Total correction","Projected amount due","Threshold / approval test","","Replacement outcome",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["Recorded scan time controls","Central recorded scan 2026-11-10 16:51 local; after 2026-11-10 16:47 local.","","","5893.42","0","5893.42","8370.459999999999","$8,370.46 is $1,119.46 above $7,251.00.","","HOLD: threshold is not met, even after approval and posting.",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["Documented physical-attempt time controls (HEADLINE)","Handheld physical attempt 2026-11-10 16:44 local; before 2026-11-10 16:47 local. Central scan posted 2026-11-10 16:51 local.","","","5893.42","3147.68","9041.1","5222.78","$5,222.78 is $2,028.22 at/below $7,251.00.","","RELEASE after Cormac approval, Tamsin posting, and Ruben verification.",""]},{"r":"23","cells":["RECOMMENDATION","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"24","cells":["Recommend the documented physical-attempt reading for the headline response. Nils Rasmussen's carrier evidence identifies the handheld capture at 2026-11-10 16:44 local as the actual delivery attempt, before the 2026-11-10 16:47 local cutoff. The central scan at 2026-11-10 16:51 local followed synchronization. The stricter scan-time reading remains visible above because the wording does not define which record is 'recorded.'","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"27","cells":["CUSTOMER-READY RESPONSE | CARSTEN HARTNETT","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"28","cells":["Dear Carsten,\n\nWe reviewed CASE-N64P and found that the same 31 TCV-9K temperature-controlled units from SHF-T83K were represented under both a receiving-reject and a carrier-return status. We will post the authorized $5,893.42 correction and, using the carrier's documented 2026-11-10 16:44 local physical attempt for the applicable cutoff determination, apply the additional $3,147.68 timing correction. The resulting amount due is $5,222.78.\n\nAfter the approved corrections are posted and the balance is verified, we will release replacement shipment SHF-R77M for 31 TCV-9K components from batch BATCH-R52 under the Monday, 2026-11-16 release plan.\n\nRegards,\nCormac Voskresensky","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"29","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"30","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"31","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"32","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"33","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"35","cells":["METHOD AND ASSUMPTIONS","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"36","cells":["Customer account and original-shipment identifiers were trimmed and uppercased before display and matching; this workbook uses DMH-Q47 and SHF-T83K. Activity entries were grouped by the source key: normalized account, normalized shipment, CASE-N64P, OL-V29, and DSP-H91. The receiving-reject and carrier-return descriptions therefore remain traceable as two source statuses for one physical case line and are counted once. The prior analyst calculation preview was excluded. The headline uses the contemporaneous handheld physical-attempt time; the later central scan remains disclosed as the alternate branch.","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"37","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"38","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"39","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Evidence","row_count":19,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["SHEAFIELD WORKS | EVIDENCE RECORD","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Drakemoor Health Network | canonical account DMH-Q47 | original shipment SHF-T83K","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Physical-line reconciliation: the activity export's rejected-at-receiving and returned-to-carrier descriptions are preserved together below as one 31-unit case line.","","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["CHRONOLOGICAL EVIDENCE RECORD","","","","",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["Event time (local)","Evidence event / source status","Canonical identifiers / case-line key","Qty / financial treatment","Source label","Review treatment"]},{"r":"7","cells":["46336.69722222222","Carrier evidence: Handheld physical delivery attempt captured at 16:44, before the stated cutoff.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","Timing fact only","Carrier timing evidence | Nils Rasmussen","Supports the physical-attempt branch."]},{"r":"8","cells":["46336.69930555556","Policy condition: Stated local cutoff under the applicable attempted-delivery wording.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","Timing condition only","Carrier timing evidence | Applicable wording","Compare with both carrier timestamps."]},{"r":"9","cells":["46336.70208333333","Carrier evidence: Central recorded scan posted at 16:51 after handheld synchronization.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","Timing fact only","Carrier timing evidence | Nils Rasmussen","Supports the recorded-scan branch."]},{"r":"10","cells":["46336.71111111111","Activity reconciliation: Source statuses: Rejected at receiving (ACT-1179, 17:04); Returned to carrier (ACT-1180, 17:05).","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","31 units\n$5,893.42 appears on each source status; reconcile one physical financial effect only.","Case activity extract | ACT-1179 + ACT-1180","One physical case line; statuses retained, not additive."]},{"r":"11","cells":["46337.3875","Customer correspondence: Carsten disputes two status descriptions for the same 31 units and asks about Monday replacement action.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","31 units\nCustomer challenges the charge","Stakeholder correspondence | Carsten Hartnett","Establishes the customer issue to resolve."]},{"r":"12","cells":["46338.3375","Replacement staging: Ruben reports SHF-R77M staged for Monday with 31 TCV-9K components from batch BATCH-R52.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91\nReplacement: SHF-R77M","31 units\nRelease remains dependent on corrected account position and approved response.","Stakeholder correspondence | Ruben Jaramillo","Carry to release plan; no release recorded."]},{"r":"13","cells":["46338.36041666667","Activity review: Prior-analyst adjusted-amount preview contains a formula error.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","No balance or correction input","Case activity extract | ACT-1183","Excluded from all calculations."]},{"r":"14","cells":["46338.38055555556","Internal correspondence: Cormac requests correction authority and a carrier-timing review before approving the response.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","No account adjustment","Stakeholder correspondence | Cormac Voskresensky","Approval follows the selected account position."]},{"r":"15","cells":["46338.49166666667","Correction authorization: ACR-L53D: $5,893.42 authorized regardless of cutoff; $3,147.68 authorized only if the cutoff condition is met.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","31 units\nOpening due $14,263.88; selected total correction $9,041.10.","Correction and release note | ACR-L53D","Selected branch applies both authorized corrections."]},{"r":"16","cells":["46339.52569444444","Scheduled commitment: Planned approval of the case response.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","Cormac approval record","Correction and release note | Committed workflow","Cormac Voskresensky; dependent on Correction authority reviewed."]},{"r":"17","cells":["46339.59930555556","Scheduled commitment: Planned posting of selected authorized corrections under ACR-L53D.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","Posting reference ACR-L53D","Correction and release note | Committed workflow","Tamsin Beaulieu; dependent on Cormac approval."]},{"r":"18","cells":["46339.67291666667","Scheduled commitment: Planned customer communication after posting confirmation.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91","Customer-send confirmation","Correction and release note | Committed workflow","Cormac Voskresensky; dependent on Posting confirmation."]},{"r":"19","cells":["46342.36180555556","Scheduled commitment: Planned verification of selected position $5,222.78 due.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91\nReplacement: SHF-R77M","Balance-verification entry","Correction and release note | Committed workflow","Ruben Jaramillo; dependent on Approved corrections posted."]},{"r":"20","cells":["46342.38680555556","Scheduled commitment: Planned release of SHF-R77M if all release conditions are met.","Customer / original: DMH-Q47 | SHF-T83K\nKey: CASE-N64P | OL-V29 | DSP-H91\nReplacement: SHF-R77M","31 units\nReplacement release record","Correction and release note | Committed workflow","Ruben Jaramillo; dependent on Approval and posting complete; amount due at or below $7,251.00."]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Release Plan","row_count":17,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["SHEAFIELD WORKS | RELEASE PLAN","","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Selected basis: documented physical attempt | Drakemoor Health Network | SHF-R77M","","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Selected branch: the 2026-11-10 16:44 local handheld physical attempt controls. Projected amount due is $5,222.78, which is $2,028.22 at/below the $7,251.00 release threshold. Release still requires approval, posted corrections, and account verification.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["","","","","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["EXECUTABLE RELEASE PLAN","","","","","",""]},{"r":"8","cells":["Step","Owner","Action","Trigger / dependency","Due (local)","Completion evidence","Instruction / outcome"]},{"r":"9","cells":["1","Cormac Voskresensky","Approve selected case response","Correction authority reviewed; use documented physical-attempt branch for the headline response.","46339.52569444444","Cormac approval record","Approve the response with $5,222.78 due and the conditional-release instruction."]},{"r":"10","cells":["2","Tamsin Beaulieu","Post authorized corrections","Cormac approval; ACR-L53D; selected physical-attempt branch qualifies the timing correction.","46339.59930555556","Posting record with ACR-L53D","Post $5,893.42 unconditional plus $3,147.68 timing correction ($9,041.10 total)."]},{"r":"11","cells":["3","Cormac Voskresensky","Send approved resolution to Carsten Hartnett","Posting confirmation; use the selected amount due and release instruction.","46339.67291666667","Customer-send confirmation","Send the customer-ready response stating $5,222.78 due and release after verification."]},{"r":"12","cells":["4","Ruben Jaramillo","Verify corrected account position","Approved corrections posted and Cormac approval confirmed; account due must be at or below $7,251.00.","46342.36180555556","Balance-verification entry showing $5,222.78 due","Confirm selected position $5,222.78 due before release."]},{"r":"13","cells":["5","Ruben Jaramillo","Release replacement SHF-R77M","Cormac approval, Tamsin posting, and Ruben verification complete; $5,222.78 due is at/below threshold.","46342.38680555556","Replacement release record: SHF-R77M, 31 TCV-9K, batch BATCH-R52","Release on Monday, 2026-11-16 by 09:17 local once all conditions are evidenced."]},{"r":"16","cells":["RELEASE RULE CHECK","","","","","",""]},{"r":"17","cells":["Selected physical-attempt branch: opening due $14,263.88 less total selected correction $9,041.10 equals $5,222.78 due. That is $2,028.22 at/below the $7,251.00 threshold. Do not release if any required approval, posting, or verification evidence is missing.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["","","","","","",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["ALTERNATE READING GUARDRAIL","","","","","",""]},{"r":"21","cells":["If the recorded central scan at 2026-11-10 16:51 local is directed to control instead, the timing correction does not apply. Amount due would be $8,370.46, above the threshold; hold SHF-R77M.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["","","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required deliverable exists as a readable XLSX file with the exact filename `Drakemoor_case_response.xlsx` at the top level of the submission.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted workbook file.","grader_hint":"Confirm the exact filename, extension, location, and that the workbook opens successfully."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains exactly three worksheets named `Case Response`, `Evidence`, and `Release Plan`.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook worksheet collection.","grader_hint":"Inspect workbook metadata and compare sheet names exactly, including spacing and capitalization."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The displayed customer account and original shipment identifiers equal the packet’s identifiers after trimming trailing spaces and normalizing letter case, and the normalized forms are used consistently throughout the workbook.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case Response, Evidence, and Release Plan identifiers.","grader_hint":"Derive canonical forms by trimming and uppercasing the identifier variants in the packet, then inspect all workbook occurrences for agreement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The case summary faithfully identifies the Drakemoor dispute, affected temperature-controlled component, original shipment, replacement shipment, affected quantity, and the reject/return overlap described in the packet.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case Response case summary.","grader_hint":"Compare each summary fact with the corresponding correspondence or case-extract fact; no unsupported product, quantity, or shipment may be substituted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Evidence sheet contains the material case events from the packet in chronological order, with event dates or times, event descriptions, and no invented event.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence timeline.","grader_hint":"Build the set of material events from the correspondence and activity extract, compare it with the submitted timeline, and verify chronological ordering."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Rows sharing the packet’s stated case-line key after identifier normalization are represented as one physical case line; the rejected and returned descriptions remain visible as overlapping source statuses, but their quantity and financial effect are not counted twice.","weight":6.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence reconciliation and correction figures.","grader_hint":"Normalize the key fields exactly as stated in the packet, group the activity records by that key, and verify that the overlapping group contributes only once while both source status descriptions remain traceable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each reconciled evidence entry identifies a source record or source section sufficiently clearly for a reviewer to trace it back to the packet.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence source labels or citations.","grader_hint":"Sample every material conclusion and verify that its Evidence entry points to the correspondence, activity extract, carrier evidence, or authorization note as applicable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The prior analyst’s erroneous calculated value is not used as a balance or correction input, and the delivered workbook contains no `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!`, `#VALUE!`, `#N/A`, or equivalent spreadsheet error value.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook cells and displayed calculations.","grader_hint":"Search formulas and cached/displayed values for error tokens, then confirm the packet’s designated prior-analyst error was not copied into any calculation or headline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The unconditional account correction equals the amount expressly authorized for the duplicate reject/return posting in the packet, with tolerance ±$0.01.","weight":6.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case Response correction section and scenario calculations.","grader_hint":"Read the unconditional authorized amount from the authorization note and compare it with every displayed unconditional correction value."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The correction documentation reproduces the packet’s authorization reference, authorizer, authorization scope, and any condition attached to the additional correction.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case Response authorization details.","grader_hint":"Compare the workbook’s authorization fields and narrative directly with Tamsin Beaulieu’s authorization note."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The cutoff-dependent correction equals the amount authorized in the packet if an on-time attempted delivery is accepted, with tolerance ±$0.01.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario comparison and correction details.","grader_hint":"Read the conditional amount from the authorization note and compare it with the event-time scenario; it must not be applied in the strict recorded-scan scenario."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Under the recorded-scan-time interpretation, the projected amount due equals the packet’s opening amount due minus only the unconditional correction, with tolerance ±$0.01.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario comparison.","grader_hint":"Calculate the strict scenario from the source opening amount and unconditional authorization; ignore the prior analyst error cell."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recorded-scan-time scenario’s release outcome follows the supplied release threshold and approval conditions using that scenario’s projected amount due.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario comparison and release recommendation.","grader_hint":"Compare the strict-scenario balance with the threshold in the release note and verify that the displayed release or hold status follows the stated condition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Under the documented physical-attempt-time interpretation, the projected amount due equals the packet’s opening amount due minus both the unconditional and cutoff-dependent corrections, with tolerance ±$0.01.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario comparison.","grader_hint":"Calculate the event-time scenario from the three source amounts and compare it with the submitted figure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The physical-attempt-time scenario’s release outcome follows the supplied release threshold and approval conditions using that scenario’s projected amount due.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario comparison and release recommendation.","grader_hint":"Compare the event-time scenario balance with the release threshold and verify that the displayed status is the corresponding policy outcome."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Both cutoff interpretations are distinctly labeled, and the workbook explicitly states which interpretation controls the headline response.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case Response scenario comparison and recommendation.","grader_hint":"Confirm that a reviewer can distinguish recorded scan time from documented physical-attempt time and identify one, not both, as the selected headline basis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A method and assumptions note of no more than 175 words discloses the identifier normalization, overlapping-line treatment, and selected cutoff interpretation sufficiently for a peer to reproduce the reconciliation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case Response method and assumptions note.","grader_hint":"Count the note’s words and assess whether all three required decisions are explicitly documented rather than merely implied."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The headline amount due, authorized corrections, recommended release status, customer response, and Release Plan all agree with the selected cutoff interpretation.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All three worksheets.","grader_hint":"Trace the selected scenario across every repeated amount and status; any contradictory balance, credit, release instruction, or customer commitment fails this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The selected cutoff interpretation is a defensible professional reading of the supplied policy and carrier evidence, and the recommendation acknowledges the decisive tradeoff rather than presenting an unsupported certainty.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation rationale and method note.","grader_hint":"Accept either interpretation if the rationale accurately addresses the pre-cutoff physical-attempt evidence, post-cutoff recorded scan, and policy wording. Do not require a particular verdict."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The customer-ready response is no more than 225 words, accurately states the finding, authorized correction, remaining amount due, and replacement next step, and avoids unnecessary internal commentary or unsupported promises.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Customer-ready response on Case Response.","grader_hint":"Count the response words, compare all facts with the selected scenario, and judge whether it could be sent to Carsten Hartnett without substantive rewriting."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Release Plan assigns the source-supported approval and correction-posting actions to Cormac Voskresensky and Tamsin Beaulieu respectively, with the correct dependency, due timing, and completion evidence.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Release Plan approval and posting entries.","grader_hint":"Compare owners, sequence, deadlines, authorization reference, and completion evidence with the correspondence and authorization note."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Ruben Jaramillo’s account-verification and replacement-release instructions identify the correct replacement shipment, quantity, release trigger, Monday timing, and evidence that release occurred.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Release Plan verification and release entries.","grader_hint":"Verify the replacement details and timing against the packet, then confirm the release trigger is consistent with the selected scenario and supplied release conditions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Release Plan includes a concrete customer-communication action for Carsten Hartnett after the account decision, with an owner, dependency, due time, and completion evidence consistent with the packet.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Release Plan communication entry.","grader_hint":"Check that communication is sequenced after the relevant approval or posting action and that its owner and timing match the supplied case record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook is professionally usable: the decision and amount due are easy to locate, labels and currency formats are clear, evidence remains readable, and the Release Plan can be acted on without reinterpretation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook and worksheet content.","grader_hint":"Review the rendered workbook as Cormac Voskresensky and Ruben Jaramillo would; award credit only if the artifact is coherent, legible, and operationally actionable despite being technically correct."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"An order clerk at Sheafield Works must resolve Drakemoor Health Network’s disputed temperature-controlled shipment charges before a replacement can be released. Cormac Voskresensky will review the response and authorize the next action.","difficulty_sources":["Normalizing customer and shipment identifiers that differ only by case or trailing spaces","De-duplicating overlapping reject and return records using the source-stated case-line key","Ignoring a residual prior-analyst formula error while preserving authoritative source facts","Choosing and consistently applying one of two defensible interpretations of a carrier scan near the cutoff"],"authoring_plan":{"reference_package":{"filename":"Drakemoor_case_packet.docx","format":"DOCX","construction":"Create one clean, text-extractable office document consolidating three semantically distinct source records: a stakeholder correspondence thread, a case activity extract, and Tamsin Beaulieu’s correction-and-release decision note. Use normal workplace formatting and clear source labels without adding a purpose-built solver rulebook.","organisations":["Sheafield Works","Drakemoor Health Network"],"people_and_roles":{"Cormac Voskresensky":"Sheafield Works reviewer with final case-response approval authority","Carsten Hartnett":"Drakemoor Health Network contact disputing the charge","Tamsin Beaulieu":"Sheafield Works account specialist who authorized the correction","Ruben Jaramillo":"Sheafield Works coordinator responsible for account verification and replacement release","Nils Rasmussen":"Carrier liaison who supplied the timing evidence"}},"source_facts":{"canonical_identifiers":{"customer_account":"DMH-Q47","case_reference":"CASE-N64P","original_shipment":"SHF-T83K","replacement_shipment":"SHF-R77M","order_line":"OL-V29","component":"TCV-9K","batch":"BATCH-R52","disposition_reference":"DSP-H91","authorization_reference":"ACR-L53D"},"identifier_variants":["Include `DMH-Q47` and `dmh-q47 ` as customer-account renderings.","Include `SHF-T83K` and `shf-t83k ` as original-shipment renderings.","State in the activity extract’s ordinary export note that account and shipment fields are trimmed and compared case-insensitively when forming the case-line key."],"case_line_key":"The source-stated key is normalized customer account, normalized shipment identifier, case reference, order line, and disposition reference.","affected_quantity":31,"financial_facts":{"opening_amount_due":14263.88,"unconditional_duplicate_posting_correction":5893.42,"cutoff_dependent_correction":3147.68,"release_threshold":7251.0},"replacement_facts":{"shipment":"SHF-R77M","component":"TCV-9K","batch":"BATCH-R52","quantity":31,"planned_release_date":"2026-11-16"},"timing_edge":{"policy_cutoff_local":"2026-11-10 16:47","handheld_physical_attempt_timestamp":"2026-11-10 16:44","central_recorded_scan_timestamp":"2026-11-10 16:51","carrier_explanation":"Nils Rasmussen confirms that the handheld captured the physical attempt before cutoff and synchronized to the central record afterward.","policy_wording":"An attempted delivery must be completed and recorded no later than the stated local cutoff.","ambiguity":"The policy does not define whether `recorded` means handheld event capture or central-system posting. Do not provide another source that resolves this distinction."},"release_rule":"After approved corrections are posted and Cormac Voskresensky approves the response, Ruben Jaramillo may release the replacement only if the remaining amount due is at or below the supplied threshold.","workflow_commitments":{"approval":"Cormac Voskresensky approves the case response by 2026-11-13 12:37 local.","posting":"Tamsin Beaulieu posts the authorized correction after approval by 2026-11-13 14:23 local and records authorization reference ACR-L53D.","communication":"Cormac Voskresensky sends the approved customer response to Carsten Hartnett by 2026-11-13 16:09 local after posting is confirmed.","release":"Ruben Jaramillo verifies the corrected amount at 2026-11-16 08:41 local and, if the selected scenario satisfies the release rule, releases SHF-R77M by 2026-11-16 09:17 local."}},"seeded_defects":{"duplicate_or_overlapping_rows":"In the case activity extract, include two records with the same normalized case-line key and the same 31 physical units. One status reads as rejected at receiving and the other as returned to carrier. Their raw account and shipment identifiers differ only by case or trailing space. The source’s ordinary key note makes clear that the records refer to one physical case line and are not additive.","residual_formula_error":"Include one prior-analyst summary cell labeled as an adjusted amount or balance whose displayed content is `#VALUE!`. All authoritative component amounts needed for reconciliation are separately present and correct. The error cell has no evidentiary authority and must be ignored rather than copied or propagated.","genuine_edge_case":"Use the physical-attempt and central-recorded scan timestamps around the stated cutoff. Treat both interpretations as valid branches: strict central recording denies the conditional correction, while handheld event time grants it. This is the only unresolved judgment edge in the packet."},"scenario_derivation":{"normalization":"Trim leading and trailing whitespace and uppercase customer-account and shipment identifiers before matching or displaying canonical identifiers.","deduplication":"Group activity entries on the complete source-stated case-line key after normalization. The rejected and returned descriptions in the overlapping group are preserved as source statuses but contribute one affected quantity and one financial effect.","recorded_scan_time_scenario":{"amount_due_rule":"Opening amount due minus the unconditional duplicate-posting correction.","conditional_correction_rule":"Do not apply the cutoff-dependent correction because the central recorded scan is after cutoff.","release_rule":"Compare the resulting amount due with the supplied release threshold after required approval and posting conditions."},"physical_attempt_time_scenario":{"amount_due_rule":"Opening amount due minus both the unconditional correction and the cutoff-dependent correction.","conditional_correction_rule":"Apply the conditional correction because the handheld evidence records the physical attempt before cutoff.","release_rule":"Compare the resulting amount due with the supplied release threshold after required approval and posting conditions."},"headline_selection":"The reference solution may select either scenario. Every headline, customer statement, correction total, and release instruction must follow the selected branch, while the alternative branch remains visible in the comparison."},"gold_generation":{"method":"Use a reference script to extract the authoritative source amounts, normalize the identifiers, group the activity entries by the stated key, and calculate both scenario balances and threshold outcomes. Separately verify copied names, identifiers, timestamps, authorization metadata, quantities, and workflow commitments against the DOCX text.","ignored_value":"Exclude the designated `#VALUE!` prior-analyst cell from every calculation and expected output.","reference_solution_choice":"For the reference workbook, select the physical-attempt-time interpretation and justify it with the contemporaneous handheld evidence while acknowledging the later central posting. The rubric must still accept a consistently applied recorded-scan-time recommendation.","hygiene_validation":"Open the finished reference workbook with an office library and scan formulas and cached values for spreadsheet errors. Render all worksheets to verify readability and actionability."},"defect_boundaries":["Do not add missing values, hidden rows, OCR-only text, conflicting quantities, unit mismatches, ambiguous dates, stale totals beyond the designated formula error, or unrelated distractor records.","Keep every graded fact text-extractable.","Do not add any additional judgment edge beyond the cutoff timestamp interpretation.","Do not include an answer key, preferred verdict, or explanatory note that resolves the cutoff ambiguity."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"ref_case_packet","filename":"Drakemoor_case_packet.docx","purpose":"Consolidated case record containing the stakeholder correspondence, case activity extract, carrier timing evidence, correction authorization, and shipment-release terms.","required":true,"discovery":"Supplied directly in the top level of the working directory."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"customer_case_response_workbook","filename":"Drakemoor_case_response.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"Customer case response workbook reconciling the evidence, documenting the authorized correction, comparing cutoff interpretations, and providing shipment-release actions.","required":true,"constraints":["Place the file at the top level of the working directory.","Use exactly the worksheets Case Response, Evidence, and Release Plan.","Customer-ready response must not exceed 225 words.","Method and assumptions note must not exceed 175 words.","All monetary values must be shown to cents.","The workbook must contain no spreadsheet error values."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"inspect_quality","work_product":"customer_case_response","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"order_clerks","sector":"wholesale_trade","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"One reviewer validates source extraction, normalization, de-duplication, and scenario arithmetic against the packet using an independent script; a second reviewer assesses the cutoff rationale, customer wording, and operational usability. Either cutoff interpretation is acceptable when explicitly selected and applied consistently.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The supplied cutoff language intentionally permits either recorded-scan time or documented physical-attempt time to control; the gold therefore contains two valid scenario branches rather than one mandatory recommendation.","Visual quality is judged for professional usability rather than against a fixed template."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:21:56+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:21:56+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:21:56+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:21:56+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/a3395850043efc03","declared_deliverables":["Drakemoor_case_response.xlsx"]};
